# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=crowns spec=warlock:destruction style=melee
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=1280x800 save=fresh. boss=crowns is a
# coverage label only -- `evening` steers at no boss (direction.md's own
# repeated note under [[#6]]) -- so this walks in at the door same as any
# other.
#
# What is actually new here: `melee` has only ever been run through THE
# VIGIL once before (2026-09-25, rogue:assassination, 844x390 touch), where
# it crossed clean in 26s -- but rogue:assassination is also the single
# fastest class in the roster (moveSpeed 178, src/sim/classes.ts:878), so
# that clean crossing has always been readable as "melee is a clean style"
# or just as "the fastest class was under the wheel," and no session has
# told the two apart. warlock:destruction sits at moveSpeed 158
# (classes.ts:812), tied for the slowest tier in the roster with
# warrior/paladin/priest -- three of whom have already stalled THE VIGIL at
# this exact 10-normal/fresh size and difficulty under other styles. Running
# `melee` on the slowest tier, on a fresh desktop viewport nobody has run
# `melee` on before, is the first test of whether the style crosses clean
# independent of class speed, or whether the one clean melee reading on
# record was actually a speed effect wearing a style's name.
open
targets
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:warlock:destruction
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot arrive-threshold

evening melee 300 6
state
bill
shot end
